user_message:
Review every unordered pair using local zero-based indices, not hypothesis IDs.
Preserve all feature fields and report exact pending alignment differences.

[
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 4,
    "feature": {
      "name": "op_asserts_absolute_certainty",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "argument"
      ],
      "definition": "OP's own argument text: 1 if the OP explicitly asserts absolute certainty about their view (e.g. cannot be wrong, no possible counterargument), else 0.",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read only the argument column (OP post body; later edits not separable). Return 1 if the OP in their own voice explicitly asserts absolute certainty or incontrovertibility of their view (e.g. 'there is no possible counterargument', 'I am 100% certain', 'undeniably', 'I can't be wrong'). Ordinary confident opinion statements without explicit absolute-certainty claims give 0. Exclude quoted external text and reported opponents' positions. This is not the complement of explicit uncertainty: a post can be 0 on both. Return null if argument is missing or empty/unparseable."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 70,
    "feature": {
      "name": "op_unwavering_certainty",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "argument"
      ],
      "definition": "OP's own argument text (not quoted others, not marked edits): 1 if the view is presented with unwavering certainty and no explicit hedging or self-doubt, else 0",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read only the argument column. Return 1 if the OP presents their view in their own voice with unwavering certainty: assertive/categorical framing (e.g. 'definitely', 'obviously', 'no doubt', flat assertions) AND no explicit hedging or self-doubt markers about their own view. Ignore quoted others and marked edits. Return 0 if any explicit hedging/self-doubt about own view is present, or if the argument is neutral/merely lacks hedging without evident certainty. Return null if argument is missing or unparseable. Do not use title, comments or conversation."
    }
  }
]

Submit {"comparisons": [...]} covering every pair with a verdict and reason.
